---
description: Dialog components use children-as-trigger and live in components/dialogs
globs: **/components/dialogs/**/*.{tsx,ts},**/components/**/*Dialog*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Dialog conventions

- Put reusable dialogs in `components/dialogs/`.
- Expose the trigger via `children` and wrap with `DialogTrigger asChild`.
- Prefer:
  `<DialogComponent><Button /></DialogComponent>`
- Avoid page-owned `open` state + separate trigger `onClick` when the dialog can manage itself.
- See `AGENTS.md` for examples.
